{
  /* The desktop package cannot use the root tsconfig, which is why the root EXCLUDES it — and why
     nothing here was typechecked at all until an unbound identifier shipped through `bun run
     typecheck` unnoticed. CI runs this config as a second step for that reason.

     The cause is that electrobun's SDK is raw TypeScript, not declarations, so importing it pulls a
     dependency's SOURCES into the program as first-class files. Neither `exclude` nor
     `skipLibCheck` keeps them out — see the root config for why — and under the root's
     `exactOptionalPropertyTypes` they emit errors we cannot fix in a dependency.

     ONE of the root's flags is genuinely blocked. Measured on electrobun 2.0.1:

       exactOptionalPropertyTypes  → 15 errors across 7 SDK files (BrowserView 7, BrowserWindow 2,
                                     Updater 2, Utils, Tray, ContextMenu, ApplicationMenu). Ours: 7.
       noUncheckedIndexedAccess    → 0 errors in electrobun. Ours: 129, ~90% of them array indexing
                                     in tests (88 in window-manager.test.ts alone).

     So `noUncheckedIndexedAccess` is off for OUR debt, not for the dependency's, and re-enabling it
     is a bounded piece of work rather than a wait. Prefer narrowing this file back toward the root
     config over widening it, and re-measure before believing either number. */
  "compilerOptions": {
    "allowImportingTsExtensions": true,
    "lib": ["ESNext", "DOM"],
    "module": "ESNext",
    "moduleResolution": "bundler",
    "noEmit": true,
    "noFallthroughCasesInSwitch": true,
    "noImplicitOverride": true,

    /* Where `electrobun/*` resolves from: the `vendor/electrobun` submodule, pinned to the exact
       release the `electrobun` devDependency names. Electrobun 2 ships no SDK on npm — every
       specifier in `node_modules/electrobun` resolves to a module that throws — and the SDK reaches
       a project only when Hutch downloads that release's core archive into `.hutch/devkit`. Pointing
       here instead means a plain `git clone` typechecks: no network, no Hutch, no `electrobun
       prepare` step in front of `tsc`.

       Hutch's `.hutch/devkit` is still the BUILD sysroot, and the two are the same release rather
       than two sources of truth — the devkit is a verbatim copy of these same directories, and
       `bun run electrobun:verify` fails when the submodule and the pin disagree. `.gitmodules`
       carries the full rationale.

       These three entries are the entire `electrobun` surface this package imports; add one here and
       to `SDK_ENTRY_POINTS` in `scripts/check-electrobun-vendor.ts` if a fourth is ever needed.
       Extending the devkit's own generated tsconfig is not an option even when one exists: it sets
       `baseUrl`, which TypeScript 7 removed, so the whole project fails with TS5102. */
    "paths": {
      "electrobun": ["../../vendor/electrobun/package/src/sdks/main/index.ts"],
      "electrobun/main": ["../../vendor/electrobun/package/src/sdks/main/index.ts"],
      "electrobun/view": ["../../vendor/electrobun/package/src/browser/index.ts"]
    },

    "resolveJsonModule": true,
    "skipLibCheck": true,
    "strict": true,
    "target": "ESNext",
    "types": ["bun-types"]
  },
  "include": ["src/**/*", "tests/**/*", "scripts/**/*", "../../types.d.ts"]
}
